{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1177860-autumn-sidhe-war-magician","id":1177860,"title":"Autumn Sidhe War-Magician","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-21T09:03:26-08:00","id":1177860,"title":"Autumn Sidhe War-Magician","content":"Greetings everyone!<br /> <br /> in one month's time, some friends and I will be in a Changeling: The Dreaming LARP (we're considering filming parts of it.) I'm having a bit of trouble crafting my character, specifically, choosing appropriate magic for the guy.<br /> <br /> What are some arts and bunks you'd recommend for an Autumn Sidhe war-magician who is a high school principal in his mortal seeming?<br /> <br /> All the best,<br /> <br /> H.F.<br /> <br /> P.S. I hope I'm not coming off as a needy tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23740-happyfimmrach","name":"HappyFimmrach","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T09:13:21-08:00","id":1177863,"title":"","content":"Are you using the Shining Host, something based off of C20, or the new beta larp rules by By Night Studios?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T10:04:21-08:00","id":1177874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1177860-autumn-sidhe-war-magician?p=1177863#post1177863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you using the Shining Host, something based off of C20, or the new beta larp rules by By Night Studios?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're using C20 with some old MET larp rules. It's been kit-bashed to Hell and back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23740,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23740-happyfimmrach","user":"HappyFimmrach","date":"01-21-2018, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23740-happyfimmrach","name":"HappyFimmrach","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T13:48:19-08:00","id":1178181,"title":"","content":"Depending where this is happenning I'm guessing he has a staff that is a yard stick / meter rule in its autumn form?<br /> <br /> As for arts, Chronos. Chronos 2 allows him to disorient his enemies to make them less effective. Chronos 4 gives him immense bonuses because he's already lived through this fight and is doing it again. It also helps him to make sure he's always walking through the school gate at 08:14:59 every morning.<br /> <br /> As for Chronos 1, forget saying &quot;It wasn't me Sir!&quot; - he can know exactly what you were doing at the time the window broke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T15:17:34-08:00","id":1178226,"title":"","content":"Sovereign, and just keep buying realms.. command mortals, cars, animals, other people's cantrips...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T14:56:35-08:00","id":1178953,"title":"","content":"Daniel Knight: A high school principal with Chronos automatically terrifies me. High school age me would have S#%^ myself inside-out!<br /> <br /> Lian: You can actually command people's cantrips? Seriously?<br /> <br /> Although an Autumn Sidhe Arts and Realms character with Sovereign <i>and </i>Chronos together would probably be terrifying as all get-out... Maybe with a bit of Primal or Dragon's Ire so nobody expects the other...<br /> <br /> <i><b>shudder</b></i><br /> <br /> All the best,<br /> <br /> H.F.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23740-happyfimmrach","name":"HappyFimmrach","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T15:36:44-08:00","id":1178974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HappyFimmrach</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1177860-autumn-sidhe-war-magician?p=1178953#post1178953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daniel Knight: A high school principal with Chronos automatically terrifies me. High school age me would have S#%^ myself inside-out!<br /> <br /> Lian: You can actually command people's cantrips? Seriously?<br /> <br /> Although an Autumn Sidhe Arts and Realms character with Sovereign <i>and </i>Chronos together would probably be terrifying as all get-out... Maybe with a bit of Primal or Dragon's Ire so nobody expects the other...<br /> <br /> <i><b>shudder</b></i><br /> <br /> All the best,<br /> <br /> H.F.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Realms make changelings scary versitile. Its not JUST Sovereign that lets you mess with other people's cantrips. Fae five(Or a point of glamour) lets you effect cantrips. You could also Mooch people's cantrips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T19:40:38-08:00","id":1179402,"title":"","content":"In all honesty there are tons of choices. Changeling Arts are pretty evenly divided into subtle and overt effects if you're using the full list in C20. The best approach is probably to think about what kind of character you want to play and then look for Arts that enhance that. None of them allow directly damaging magical attacks that are reachable by a starting character anyway. So it really is just going to be style and swordplay (or some equivalent) for awhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23656-lanir","name":"Lanir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T22:18:49-08:00","id":1179440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1177860-autumn-sidhe-war-magician?p=1179402#post1179402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty there are tons of choices. Changeling Arts are pretty evenly divided into subtle and overt effects if you're using the full list in C20. The best approach is probably to think about what kind of character you want to play and then look for Arts that enhance that. None of them allow directly damaging magical attacks that are reachable by a starting character anyway. So it really is just going to be style and swordplay (or some equivalent) for awhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Treasure's a hell of a thing, letting you start with lightning guns, staves of ice, wands of fireball etc..<br /> <br /> Unleashing IS also a hell of a thing letting you move beyond the powers you have and even create new ones so don't discount what someone can do.<br /> <br /> That said you start with 3 arts you can put in a single art. SO starting with level 3. It costs 10 Freebie points from there to max any one art. You start with 15 and can get up to 22.<br /> <br /> Of course he might be using some MET system which have different Freebie points.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T23:47:26-08:00","id":1179764,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I got another one.<br /> <br /> Naming 1: He can decypher teen slang and code words. Faliborget salibomething lalibike thalibis.<br /> <br /> Naming 2: &quot;You are going to be Mr Politeness for the rest of this semester, or I will make your life a living hell!&quot; - with 4 successes means that for a month you cannot regain willpower unless you're being polite. Substitute whatever the person has shown a lack of.<br /> <br /> Edit: On a more positive note, Chronos 4 also means that when the ambulance gets called because some boys were playing on the roof and one of them fell, he can rewind time long enough to catch them before the fall happens. They won't think they got lucky but they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13395,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","user":"Daniel Knight","date":". 01-27-2018, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}